  "notes": "The same entity as Home Assistant 2026.10.4 sends it with unit_system us_customary: openweathermap.json's values fed to Home Assistant's WeatherEntity as native values in the units its attributes state (°C, hPa, km/h, km, mm), state and forecasts read back through the weather component with hass.config.units set to US_CUSTOMARY_SYSTEM. Temperatures come back as whole °F (ints: outside °C the weather entity rounds to whole degrees), pressure in inHg, wind in mph, visibility in mi and precipitation in in, each to 2 decimals; humidity, bearings, conditions, datetimes and every other field are as in the metric file. The metric file's notes follow; their numbers are metric. State is the core snapshot of the default 'v3.0' mode (One Call 3.0). Forecasts were built from source (weather.py, coordinator.py and the pyopenweathermap library). Daily is the test's mock entry run through that code (values changed below); the mock's hourly list is empty, so hourly here is 48 realistic One Call hours with exactly the fields the code sets. One Call's hourly list starts at the top of the current hour, so in live use the first entry is up to 59 minutes old; One Call daily entries are stamped 12:00 local time, while the mock's daily entry carries the observation time. Daily has no apparent_temperature: the code passes the API's feels_like object (morning/day/evening/night) and the entity drops it. Daily precipitation is rain plus snow; hourly precipitation is rain plus snow for the hour, 0 when the API sends neither, so it is always present. precipitation_probability is the API's 0-1 'pop' turned into a whole percent, 0 when absent. wind_gust_speed only when the API sends a gust; uv_index is a float. Weather code 800 becomes sunny or clear-night by whether the sun is up at the time of the update, not at the entry's time, so every clear hour in a forecast shows the same one (here sunny, even at night). Codes missing from the integration's map (e.g. 321, 531, 613, 781) give condition null, and the state 'unknown'. Mode 'current' (free tier) has no supported_features attribute and no forecasts. Mode 'forecast' (free tier) has supported_features 2: hourly only, in 3-hour steps for 5 days, precipitation taken from the 3 h totals, no dew_point and uv_index null, and no current conditions at all, so its state is 'unknown' with only the unit attributes (the core snapshot for that mode shows conditions only because the test's mock supplies them). The minute forecast is a separate openweathermap.get_minute_forecast service in v3.0 mode, not part of weather.get_forecasts. Changes for realism: the test's daily mock (21.3/8.1 C, dew point 11.3 C, 1015 hPa) did not fit its own current conditions (6.8 C, 1000 hPa, a raw windy April afternoon); today is now 7.6/1.8 C, 1001 hPa, dew point 0.8 (from 7.6 C and 62 %). The made-up hourly dew points ran about 0.5-1 C low for their temperature and humidity; 43 of 48 are recomputed from them.",
